          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "\n- **The International School @ ParkCity (ISPH):** British curriculum, with a newer campus on the western side of the city.\n\n**Language-specific schools**\n\n- **Lycée Français Alexandre Yersin:** Follows the French national curriculum (AEFE network), so it's the obvious choice for French-speaking families.\n- There are also Japanese and Korean schools for those communities.\n\n**One caution:** BVIS Hanoi, Wellspring and similar schools are excellent, but they're bilingual and mostly Vietnamese. They may suit you if you want deep local integration, but they're a different experience from a mainly expat school.\n\n**How to narrow it down**\n\n1. **Where you'll live:** Hanoi traffic is bad, so a long school run is painful. "
