            "type": "text",
            "text": " Families in Ciputra are close to UNIS and Hanoi Academy. Those in Long Bien or Vinhomes Riverside are near BIS.\n2. **Where you'll move next:** If you might move again, IB schools like UNIS, HIS or Hanoi Academy make transfers easiest. If you're heading back to the UK, BIS or ISPH fit best. For North America, Concordia or SPASH fit best.\n3. **Budget:** Top-tier fees can be well over US$25,000–35,000 a year for older grades. Check what's included, such as the bus, lunch, enrolment fees and building levies. Also find out whether your employer pays.\n4. **Waitlists:** UNIS and BIS can fill up in some year groups, so apply early, ideally 6–12 months ahead.\n5. **Visit or do a virtual tour:** Ask about class sizes, how much staff turnover there is, how they handle air quality (indoor air filtration and policies for high-pollution days matter in Hanoi), and what support they offer for special learning needs.\n\nIf you tell me your children's ages, your nationality or next likely move, your budget and roughly where you'll live, I can narrow this to two or three schools."
